export default {"format":"cadcraft-help","version":1,"app":"bimcraft","addon":"pointcloud","name":"Point clouds","sections":{"start":"Getting started","tasks":"Walkthroughs","switching":"Coming from other software","reference":"Reference","trouble":"Troubleshooting and limits"},"topics":[{"slug":"point-clouds-here","scope":"addon:pointcloud","title":"Point clouds in BimCraft and CadCraft","summary":"With the Point clouds add-on, open a LAS, LAZ, E57, PLY, PCD, PTX, XYZ or PTS cloud of millions of points, see all of it in the app's 3D view, clean it with a lasso or box, and cut a section through it.","section":"tasks","order":63,"keywords":["point cloud","las","laz","e57","ply","pcd","ptx","xyz","pts","scan","lidar","clean","lasso","noise","classify","ground","section","3d","add-on","tiles"],"headings":[{"id":"open-a-cloud","text":"Open a cloud","level":2},{"id":"where-it-sits","text":"Where it sits","level":2},{"id":"clean-it","text":"Clean it","level":2},{"id":"sort-it-bimcraft-only","text":"Sort it (BimCraft only)","level":2},{"id":"section-strip","text":"Section strip","level":2},{"id":"not-built-yet","text":"Not built yet","level":2}],"html":"\u003Cp\u003EMost people never need this, so it is an add-on. Switch on \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EPoint clouds\u003C/span\u003E in Settings › Add-ons; a \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EPoint clouds\u003C/span\u003E tab (BimCraft) or section (CadCraft) appears in the right-hand panel. The file is read in your browser and the tiles are kept in this browser&#039;s own storage, or in a folder you pick; nothing is uploaded.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Caside class=\"hc hc-warning\"\u003E\u003Cp class=\"hc-label\"\u003EWarning\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EEverything this tab reports is a number from your data, not a certificate. It was tested on a made-up site and on small made-up files in each app, not on a real scan: read the first results with care and tell us what you find.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/aside\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIt is the same add-on as in CivilCraft, with the same engine; only the part that draws in the app&#039;s own 3D view differs. The app&#039;s older Attach / Place / Register scan tools are separate and unchanged.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"open-a-cloud\"\u003EOpen a cloud\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOpen a model first in BimCraft (the 3D view is made with the first model), or the 3D tab in CadCraft. Under \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EOpen a cloud\u003C/span\u003E choose a file. LAS and LAZ are tiled as they are. E57, PLY, PCD, PTX, XYZ and PTS are read by the app&#039;s own reader first, at most 3 million points kept (thinned evenly, the tab says so), then tiled the same way. Metres are assumed unless the file says feet. Press \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EBuild the cloud\u003C/span\u003E; a build can be stopped and resumed (LAS and LAZ).\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"where-it-sits\"\u003EWhere it sits\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe cloud is drawn in the 3D view with coarse tiles that refine as you move closer, never more than \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EMost points drawn\u003C/span\u003E at once. If the cloud&#039;s own coordinates overlap the model (or drawing), it is drawn where its numbers say, so a registered scan lines up with the design; otherwise it is centred on the model or drawing with its lowest point on the ground. Eye-dome lighting starts off in these apps: tick it to try.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"clean-it\"\u003EClean it\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EClean\u003C/span\u003E takes a lasso, a box or a polygon drawn over the 3D view (a vertical prism down to the cloud&#039;s middle height: use the Top view when it has to be exact), changes the class of the points inside, deletes them, restores them or crops to them. A noise filter finds stray points. Every step is one undo.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"sort-it-bimcraft-only\"\u003ESort it (BimCraft only)\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EClassify\u003C/span\u003E finds the ground and then the geometric classes (low, medium and high vegetation, buildings), tile by tile. CadCraft does not have it: it carries no TIN or ground modules, and an add-on may not reach into another folder.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"section-strip\"\u003ESection strip\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESection strip\u003C/span\u003E draws a line across the cloud and shows the points within a width of it, seen from the side.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"not-built-yet\"\u003ENot built yet\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EBuilding the ground into the model, contours, stockpile and flight-to-flight volumes, the orthomosaic drape and the plan raster are CivilCraft&#039;s; they are not in these two apps.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECadCraft has no Classify.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA very large E57 or PLY is read whole before tiling, so it takes a while and keeps only 3 million points.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo change of coordinate system: metres assumed.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","text":"Most people never need this, so it is an add-on. Switch on Point clouds in Settings › Add-ons; a Point clouds tab (BimCraft) or section (CadCraft) appears in the right-hand panel. The file is read in your browser and the tiles are kept in this browser's own storage, or in a folder you pick; nothing is uploaded. Everything this tab reports is a number from your data, not a certificate. It was tested on a made-up site and on small made-up files in each app, not on a real scan: read the first results with care and tell us what you find. It is the same add-on as in CivilCraft, with the same engine; only the part that draws in the app's own 3D view differs. The app's older Attach / Place / Register scan tools are separate and unchanged. Open a cloud Open a model first in BimCraft (the 3D view is made with the first model), or the 3D tab in CadCraft. Under Open a cloud choose a file. LAS and LAZ are tiled as they are. E57, PLY, PCD, PTX, XYZ and PTS are read by the app's own reader first, at most 3 million points kept (thinned evenly, the tab says so), then tiled the same way. Metres are assumed unless the file says feet. Press Build the cloud; a build can be stopped and resumed (LAS and LAZ). Where it sits The cloud is drawn in the 3D view with coarse tiles that refine as you move closer, never more than Most points drawn at once. If the cloud's own coordinates overlap the model (or drawing), it is drawn where its numbers say, so a registered scan lines up with the design; otherwise it is centred on the model or drawing with its lowest point on the ground. Eye-dome lighting starts off in these apps: tick it to try. Clean it Clean takes a lasso, a box or a polygon drawn over the 3D view (a vertical prism down to the cloud's middle height: use the Top view when it has to be exact), changes the class of the points inside, deletes them, restores them or crops to them. A noise filter finds stray points. Every step is one undo. Sort it (BimCraft only) Classify finds the ground and then the geometric classes (low, medium and high vegetation, buildings), tile by tile. CadCraft does not have it: it carries no TIN or ground modules, and an add-on may not reach into another folder. Section strip Section strip draws a line across the cloud and shows the points within a width of it, seen from the side. Not built yet Building the ground into the model, contours, stockpile and flight-to-flight volumes, the orthomosaic drape and the plan raster are CivilCraft's; they are not in these two apps. CadCraft has no Classify. A very large E57 or PLY is read whole before tiling, so it takes a while and keeps only 3 million points. No change of coordinate system: metres assumed."}]};
